Default map (capacity 16):
   1 keys in one bucket -> capacity 16, bucket type Node
   2 keys in one bucket -> capacity 16, bucket type Node
   3 keys in one bucket -> capacity 16, bucket type Node
   4 keys in one bucket -> capacity 16, bucket type Node
   5 keys in one bucket -> capacity 16, bucket type Node
   6 keys in one bucket -> capacity 16, bucket type Node
   7 keys in one bucket -> capacity 16, bucket type Node
   8 keys in one bucket -> capacity 16, bucket type Node
   9 keys in one bucket -> capacity 32, bucket type Node
  10 keys in one bucket -> capacity 64, bucket type Node
  11 keys in one bucket -> capacity 64, bucket type TreeNode
  Below 64 buckets HashMap RESIZES instead of treeifying — a long chain in a small
  table usually means the table is too small, not that the hash is bad.

Pre-sized map (capacity 64):
   8 keys in one bucket -> capacity 64, bucket type Node
   9 keys in one bucket -> capacity 64, bucket type TreeNode
